/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Breast cancer is classified as the most common cause of death among malignant tumour diseases. ER-alpha accounts for 60% of cases of breast cancer including both luminal A and luminal B subtypes. Endocrine resistance has been reckoned as a factor for high mortality in patients of Breast cancer. The aim of this study is to find new compounds by building Quantitative Structure Activity Relationship \(QSAR\) model to screen the best drugs or compounds that have the potential to act as an agonist to GR. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
