/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Most of the previous research conducted is based on treatment via hormonal therapy, primarily on tamoxifen. This drug has been used as a potent treatment for the last 40 years. Unfortunately, resistance against it is one serious drawback.  Most of the conducted research has been carried out via in vitro experimentation.  However, little research has been carried out in drug discovery via in silico techniques  which makes our study somewhat unique. Our study intends to screen for active compounds that can be modified into new drug  therapies against breast cancer using Quantitative Structure Activity Relationship  \(QSAR\) technique. QSAR modeling includes all the statistical methods by which biological activities,  expressed by logarithms of equipotent molar activities are related with structural  elements, physiochemical properties, or fields. This technique describes connections  between the structure activities of molecules in quantitative way \(Ilaghi-Hoseini &  Garkani-Nejad, 2022a\). It links the structural properties of compounds with biological  activities in such a way that any change in structural properties causes variation in  biological activities of compounds. Furthermore, QSAR descriptors can be used to )
