/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Pharmacoinformatic is a rapidly growing field that combines the principles of computer science, pharmacology, biology, and chemistry in developing new drugs or increasing the efficacy of existing drugs. Advanced computational tools and techniques can be used to interpret and analyze biological data, chemical structures, and drug interactions to facilitate drug discovery and development \(Amin et al., 2017\). Breast cancer is a significant health concern globally and is the leading cause of cancer-related deaths among women. The glucocorticoid receptor is a nuclear hormone receptor protein that is essential in the formation, growth, and progression of breast cancer. As a result, GR agonists have emerged as a prospective therapeutic target for the treatment of breast cancer. )
/Pg 23 0 R
