788 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Breast cancer is a growing health concern among women worldwide, particularly in Pakistan where the rate of breast cancer is highest in comparison to the rest of Asian countries \(Saeed et al., 2021\). According to \(Mubarik et al., 2019\), one-ninth of Pakistani women are facing this disease and they suggest that there has been a 98.6% increase in cancer incidence among women. Younger women from rural areas of Pakistan remain at high risk of developing hereditary breast cancer because of prevalent consanguineous marriages. Another study conducted in Karachi, Pakistan, \(Zaheer et al., 2019\) suggests that the breast cancer incidence rate is expected to increase from 23.1% in 2020 to 60.7% in 2025. This research has also emphasized that breast cancer diagnoses in younger women of ages 30 to 34 will increase from 70.7% to 130.6% in 2020 to 2025 relative to 2015. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
