/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (One critical mechanism of GR resistance is the activation of alternative signaling pathways that bypass glucocorticoid dependency, enabling breast cancer cell growth and survival independent of GR. For instance, the PI3K/Akt/mTOR pathway is frequently upregulated in GR-resistant breast cancer cells, driving cell survival and proliferation under therapeutic stress \(Dwyer et al., 2023\). Additionally, loss or mutation of GR can contribute to resistance. Breast cancer cells may downregulate GR expression, rendering GR-targeted therapies ineffective. Alternatively, mutations in GR or its downstream effectors can lead to constitutive receptor activation, making it insensitive to therapeutic inhibition \(Thakur et al., 2024\). Other resistance mechanisms include alterations in co- regulators modulating GR activity, changes in glucocorticoid metabolism, and the presence of cancer stem cells that evade GR-targeted treatments. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
