/T (Combinatorial therapies involving GR modulation are also promising. In prostate cancer,  targeting the GR signature gene Mono Amine Oxidase-A \(MAO-A\) alongside  chemotherapy or anti-androgen therapies \(e.g., enzalutamide\) has improved treatment  efficacy. MAO-A inhibitors, already used for affective disorders, enhance the effectiveness  of these treatments by counteracting GR-driven resistance. Additionally, combining GR  antagonists like Lestaurtinib with cisplatin in solid tumors addresses chemotherapy  resistance by inhibiting MAO-A-induced suppression of pro-apoptotic genes like Bim,  restoring sensitivity to platinum-based drugs. )
/E (Combinatorial therapies involving GR modulation are also promising. In prostate cancer,  targeting the GR signature gene Mono Amine Oxidase-A \(MAO-A\) alongside  chemotherapy or anti-androgen therapies \(e.g., enzalutamide\) has improved treatment  efficacy. MAO-A inhibitors, already used for affective disorders, enhance the effectiveness  of these treatments by counteracting GR-driven resistance. Additionally, combining GR  antagonists like Lestaurtinib with cisplatin in solid tumors addresses chemotherapy  resistance by inhibiting MAO-A-induced suppression of pro-apoptotic genes like Bim,  restoring sensitivity to platinum-based drugs. )
