/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (While molecular docking is a fast and cost-effective method to gain insight into the binding interaction of a compound with its target protein, it requires accurate three- dimensional structural knowledge of the target and the ligand which may not always be available. Molecular docking also ignores some important characteristics in determining binding affinity such as dynamic protein-ligand interactions and the impact of solvation \(Meng et al., 2011\). Therefore, this technique should be applied in combination with other in-silico approaches such as QSAR modeling. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
