892 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A relatively new in-silico approach used in modern drug discovery is quantitative structure-activity relationship \(QSAR\) modeling. These models use a ligand-based approach and can predict the biological activity of novel compounds based on their molecular structure and properties. QSAR models assume that a compound's biological activity is determined by its physicochemical properties, which can be correlated with its biological activity using mathematical models \(Piir et al., 2018\). QSAR models can be used in breast cancer research to predict the efficacy and toxicity of novel compounds against breast cancer cell lines. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
