/E (Developing a reliable QSAR model relies heavily on using freely available chemical and bioactivity databases such as PubChem, ChEMBL and BindingDB. Thchemicals, physicochemical information and bioactive results, PubChem makes it easy to spot possible active compounds. If you want to build predictive models, ChEMBL is important as it includes detailed details about drug-like molecules, their activities, targets and experiments. BindingDB gives access to measured protein-ligand binding affinities which help show interactions between molecules with more accuracy. Combined, the databases supply the right data necessary for constructing precise and accurate QSAR models. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [9 10]
