1055 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The relevant molecular descriptors in the data set were chosen as feature for model training after data cleaning and Ro5 filtering. Dimensionality reduction by feature extraction and selection is essential to reduce the number of features, avoid overfitting and improve model performance. While there are techniques such as recursive feature elimination, principal component analysis \(PCA\) or correlation-based feature selection that can be used to identify the most informative descriptors and remove redundant or irrelevant ones \(Guyon & Elisseeff, 2003\) such techniques can impose additional costs to the runtime of the learning process. This step improves computational efficiency and model interpretability \(particularly important when dealing with high-dimensional descriptor datasets typical for QSAR studies\). )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
