1058 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The dataset was partitioned into training and testing subsets \(typically as 80:20 split\) to evaluate the generalizability and robustness of the QSAR model. This stratified splitting makes sure that active and inactive compounds are proportionally present in both subsets and hence will not lead to data imbalance that could bias model evaluation. The model is fit to the training set and its predictive accuracy is assessed on unseen data \(i.e. the independent test set\) \(Hastie, Tibshirani, & Friedman, 2009\). This enables to validate the practical utility of the model in drug discovery applications. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
