1089 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A baseline model was developed using Random Forest Regression, and a mean 10-fold validation was performed. The mean 10-fold validation technique divided our training data into ten equal parts, using nine of these parts to train the model while the tenth was used to validate the model. This process was repeated five times, according to the machine learning algorithm, each time a different part of the data was used as the validation set. The mean of the performance metric across all five validation sets was calculated as Mean 5-fold RMSE score. The random forest regression of the 33% test dataset was also calculated as RMSE test set score. A third RMSE score was obtained by randomizing the target variable in the test set, so it is not the same as those in the training dataset. This evaluated the performance of our model and its robustness using a set of  26 )
/E (A baseline model was developed using Random Forest Regression, and a mean 10-fold validation was performed. The mean 10-fold validation technique divided our training data into ten equal parts, using nine of these parts to train the model while the tenth was used to validate the model. This process was repeated five times, according to the machine learning algorithm, each time a different part of the data was used as the validation set. The mean of the performance metric across all five validation sets was calculated as Mean 5-fold RMSE score. The random forest regression of the 33% test dataset was also calculated as RMSE test set score. A third RMSE score was obtained by randomizing the target variable in the test set, so it is not the same as those in the training dataset. This evaluated the performance of our model and its robustness using a set of  26 )
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [3]
>>
