/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The Random Forrest Model\(RFM\) Regression Model is a linear regression model that seeks the best-fitting line across a set of data points by minimizing the sum of squared discrepancies between anticipated and actual values. In our case, the data points are the predicted EC 50 and experimental EC50 values of the dependent variable.  RFM regression model generated the following values for Train and Test Dataset. The R-squared value for the train and test data was 0.609 and 0.645 respectively. A model  will be considered within the range of moderate to strong fit if the R-squared value is  between 0.6 to 0.9. The adjacent R-squared value for the train data was reported as 0.604  and the F-statistic value was reported as 126.6. This F-statistic model shows that the  model is statistically significant as a larger F-statistic value is preferred as it indicates the  overall significance of the regression model. The adjusted R-squared value ranges from  negative to 1 with the values closest to 1 preferred as it indicates that the model is a better  fit for the data \(Chicco et al., 2021\). )
/E (The Random Forrest Model\(RFM\) Regression Model is a linear regression model that seeks the best-fitting line across a set of data points by minimizing the sum of squared discrepancies between anticipated and actual values. In our case, the data points are the predicted EC 50 and experimental EC50 values of the dependent variable.  RFM regression model generated the following values for Train and Test Dataset. The R-squared value for the train and test data was 0.609 and 0.645 respectively. A model  will be considered within the range of moderate to strong fit if the R-squared value is  between 0.6 to 0.9. The adjacent R-squared value for the train data was reported as 0.604  and the F-statistic value was reported as 126.6. This F-statistic model shows that the  model is statistically significant as a larger F-statistic value is preferred as it indicates the  overall significance of the regression model. The adjusted R-squared value ranges from  negative to 1 with the values closest to 1 preferred as it indicates that the model is a better  fit for the data \(Chicco et al., 2021\). )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
