/T (The drug-protein interactions are explained through resultant docking and confidence scores. Typically, when a score is above 0.7, the drug is very likely to bind with the receptor. However, if the obtained confidence score is between the range of 0.5-0.7, there is a possibility that the drug will bind to the receptor. But any confidence score obtained below 0.5 indicates that it is highly unlikely that the drug will bind to the target receptor protein \(Yan et al., 2020\). )
