1208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The machine learning built based on PLS was classified via validation model of MLR and SVM, where PLS and SVM generated same values for the Train and Test sets, i.e., 0.804 and 0.814 respectively \(Thakur et al., 2022; van de Waterbeemd, 2008\). Providing sufficient validation for the created model. The linear plot, generated from both algorithms to check the predictive ability of the QSAR model, showed very similar values for predicted pEC50 and experimentally determined pEC50 values further highlighting the accuracy of the predictability of the model.  A statistical method, OLS, was used to further analyze the cross validity of the model. The  higher R2 and F values with lower RMSE values highlights the predictive ability of the  model \(Khan & Roy, 2018; Pourbasheer et al., 2019\). According to a study \(Ozili, 2023\),  R2 value falling between 0.50-0.90 is considered significant, resulting in best fit model.  The generated values of R2 \(0.609\), Adj R2\(0.604\), and F-statistic \(126.6\) for the train  datasets and R2 \(0.645\), and Adj R2\(0.636\) are considered optimal for both sets,  indicating an appropriate predictive ability of the built model \(Thakur et al., 2022\). To meet one of our aims, i.e., repurposing of the drug compounds for treatment, the model  was tested on unknown FDA approved drug compounds to find potential drugs \(hits\) for  agonist against GR. This was followed by molecular docking of mutant receptors against  the hits obtained to validate our model.  The docking score, confidence score and conventional H-bonds are considered the three  most important features in the docking results. More negative docking score along with  high binding energy/high confidence score is preferred as it increase the possibility of  binding between the drug hits and the mutant receptors \(Ilaghi-Hoseini & Garkani-Nejad,  2022b\). Conventional H-bonds are the most stable bonds so a drug-receptor complex  having one or two Hydrogen bonds is preferable. Our results further validate our model  performance as all the hits that were obtained have high possibility of binding to the  chosen mutant receptors but if we were to select the most stable drug-receptor complex  that would be Cabozantinib, because it formed complex with nearly all mutated protein  receptors with relatively higher negative docking score, higher confidence score, and at  most all the formed complex has minimum one conventional H-bond in them, except for  Cabozantinib-5W98 model. Followed by Cabozantinib, Vecuronium Bromide also gave  optimum scores for docking score, confidence score and conventional H-bond. In )
/E (The machine learning built based on PLS was classified via validation model of MLR and SVM, where PLS and SVM generated same values for the Train and Test sets, i.e., 0.804 and 0.814 respectively \(Thakur et al., 2022; van de Waterbeemd, 2008\). Providing sufficient validation for the created model. The linear plot, generated from both algorithms to check the predictive ability of the QSAR model, showed very similar values for predicted pEC50 and experimentally determined pEC50 values further highlighting the accuracy of the predictability of the model.  A statistical method, OLS, was used to further analyze the cross validity of the model. The  higher R2 and F values with lower RMSE values highlights the predictive ability of the  model \(Khan & Roy, 2018; Pourbasheer et al., 2019\). According to a study \(Ozili, 2023\),  R2 value falling between 0.50-0.90 is considered significant, resulting in best fit model.  The generated values of R2 \(0.609\), Adj R2\(0.604\), and F-statistic \(126.6\) for the train  datasets and R2 \(0.645\), and Adj R2\(0.636\) are considered optimal for both sets,  indicating an appropriate predictive ability of the built model \(Thakur et al., 2022\). To meet one of our aims, i.e., repurposing of the drug compounds for treatment, the model  was tested on unknown FDA approved drug compounds to find potential drugs \(hits\) for  agonist against GR. This was followed by molecular docking of mutant receptors against  the hits obtained to validate our model.  The docking score, confidence score and conventional H-bonds are considered the three  most important features in the docking results. More negative docking score along with  high binding energy/high confidence score is preferred as it increase the possibility of  binding between the drug hits and the mutant receptors \(Ilaghi-Hoseini & Garkani-Nejad,  2022b\). Conventional H-bonds are the most stable bonds so a drug-receptor complex  having one or two Hydrogen bonds is preferable. Our results further validate our model  performance as all the hits that were obtained have high possibility of binding to the  chosen mutant receptors but if we were to select the most stable drug-receptor complex  that would be Cabozantinib, because it formed complex with nearly all mutated protein  receptors with relatively higher negative docking score, higher confidence score, and at  most all the formed complex has minimum one conventional H-bond in them, except for  Cabozantinib-5W98 model. Followed by Cabozantinib, Vecuronium Bromide also gave  optimum scores for docking score, confidence score and conventional H-bond. In )
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
