1210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (comparison Amiodarone and Verapamil drugs are predicted to be relatively poor inhibitors of ER protein receptors.  By constructing a QSAR model based on their experimental data, our team was able to  effectively predict the bioactivity of unknown compounds. Our QSAR model made these  predictions using a collection of chemical descriptors, and its validation findings  demonstrated that it was highly predictive. We were able to assess the model's  effectiveness by comparing its predictions to the actual bioactivity values of a test set of  compounds that had not been employed in the model's development. This validation  approach demonstrated that the model could accurately predict the bioactivity of these  compounds. We also utilized our QSAR model to find pharmacological hits with potential  binding and agonist activity for GR. These hits were chosen based on their projected  bioactivity, and we next investigated their binding potential to the target protein using  molecular docking experiments. These investigations' high docking scores supported our  model's prediction capabilities and offered more evidence of its ability to forecast the  bioactivity of unknown compounds. )
/E (comparison Amiodarone and Verapamil drugs are predicted to be relatively poor inhibitors of ER protein receptors.  By constructing a QSAR model based on their experimental data, our team was able to  effectively predict the bioactivity of unknown compounds. Our QSAR model made these  predictions using a collection of chemical descriptors, and its validation findings  demonstrated that it was highly predictive. We were able to assess the model's  effectiveness by comparing its predictions to the actual bioactivity values of a test set of  compounds that had not been employed in the model's development. This validation  approach demonstrated that the model could accurately predict the bioactivity of these  compounds. We also utilized our QSAR model to find pharmacological hits with potential  binding and agonist activity for GR. These hits were chosen based on their projected  bioactivity, and we next investigated their binding potential to the target protein using  molecular docking experiments. These investigations' high docking scores supported our  model's prediction capabilities and offered more evidence of its ability to forecast the  bioactivity of unknown compounds. )
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
